Sval: remove the Learn more links that have no page on Sval's site

app.support.baseURL is Sval's support address, and Firefox's UI appends a
support article's slug to it. Sval's site has a page for some of those
slugs; these links name one it has none for, so they would open a page
that does not exist. Each link goes, and the setting, notice, panel or
error page around it stays: Picture-in-Picture, spell checking and
Windows single sign-on in settings, the decoder and speech-dispatcher
notices, the add-on permissions policy banner, the data loss prevention
panel, and the certificate time errors and site-not-found error pages.

With no time-errors link left, the bundled offline copy of that article,
which NetErrorParent shows when the article's address fails to load, has
no way in, so it is not packaged.

